  "details": "I can't figure out why this string variable won't sync:\n  /// <summary>\n  /// The user's world IDs ordered in a useable compressed array, compressed into a string for syncing.\n  /// EX: 1/5/4/6/7/8/\n  /// </summary>\n  [UdonSynced(UdonSyncMode.None)] public string compressedUserIDs = \"\";\nUpdate function::\n  void Update() {\nSendCustomNetworkEvent(VRC.Udon.Common.Interfaces.NetworkEventTarget.All, \"updateDebugText\");\n  }\nUpdate network call:\n  \n  /// <summary>\n  /// update the debug text object\n  /// </summary>\n  public void updateDebugText() {\n    if (debugText != null && !string.IsNullOrEmpty(compressedUserIDs)) {\n      string playerList = \"\";\n      int playerIndex = 0;\n      foreach (string worldID in getPlayerWorldIDs()) {\n        if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(worldID)) {\n          playerList += playerIndex.ToString() + \": \" + getPlayer(playerIndex).displayName + \"(\" + worldID + \"), \";\n        } else {\n          playerList += playerIndex.ToString() + \": EMPTY(-1), \";\n        }\n        playerIndex++;\n      }\n      debugText.text = \"User List:\\n\" + playerList;\n    } else {\n      if (debugText != null) {\n        debugText.text = \"waiting on manager to load players\";\n      }\n    }\n  }\nI'm using this test before editing the synced variable as well:\nNetworking.IsOwner(Networking.LocalPlayer, gameObject)\nWhat am I missing? Why won't the variable sync? I can even see in debug that the variable is not synced between the logs.",
